11. CONCLUSION
A3 defines the plan representation that DECOMPOSE produces and EXECUTE consumes.
Combined with A4, the two load-bearing premises of the Verifiable Agency Theorem are now
in place:
· A4 — finite state and world model.
· A3 — finite plan library with bounded plans.
With these, the Verifiable Agency Theorem's assumptions (A2, A3, A4 in the proof) are
grounded. The theorem becomes dischargeable.
The three commitments:
1. Plans are finite. By construction, not by hope.
2. Plans are bounded. Every plan has |p| ≤ K.
3. Plans are compositional but not recursive. DAG-only, compile-time composition.
These commitments, together with A4, make the agentic architecture complete at the
specification level.
